    (required-information "Capabilities: machine-operations, target-description; analyses: liveness-analysis. Results must be current.")
    (transformation "Replace (move register register) with (removed-move) when the declared proof obligations hold. Preserve source provenance and update uses and edges consistently.")
    (semantic-assumptions "Same register names do not imply a no-op: reject moves that zero upper lanes, alter flags, or carry effects.")
    (correctness "Preserve required observable behavior under the declared execution model; unknown facts never justify the rewrite.")
    (known-limitations "Declarative contract only; NodeIR matching and execution require an external adapter. Same register names do not imply a no-op: reject moves that zero upper lanes, alter flags, or carry effects.")
    (expected-effects "Simplifies the matched representation; runtime benefit and code-size change depend on the surrounding program and target.")
    (testing-strategy "tests/test_catalog.py checks positive, rejected, unknown, invalidated, and stage-mismatch applicability for blackstone.lir.registers.redundant-register-move. Integer-model tests cover HIR identities; other transformations have no executable NodeIR evidence.")
    (references "Blackstone AGENTS.md sections 4, 5, 11, 12, 17, and 18; tools/blackstone/README.md contract semantics.")
